      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-134944",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/f9/f9fee649d91712018b3888f2b982556b0a2d7371c3b186c4275133ccb2337a20.png)\n\nThe semi-log scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the population of an ant colony $(y)$ and the time, in years, since the colony was first established $(x)$. The equation of the trend line is $Y = 3 + 0.2x$. Estimate the population of the colony after $12$ years. Round your answer to the nearest ten thousand.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
