      ":question/problem": "![](images/9f/9ff00227b4f4d9621e05c6b39b1cef7b1afefdd87533ef5a457441a3dcf369d3.png)\n\nThe semi-log scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the amount of a drug, in milligrams, in a patient's bloodstream $(y)$ and the time, in hours, since the patient first ingested it $(x)$. The equation of the trend line is $Y = 2 - 0.1x$. How long does it take for the amount of drug in the patient's bloodstream to reduce to $50$ milligrams?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
